## Don't-repeat-these-mistakes log (updated)

All entries from `AXIOMS_TODO.md` §5 still apply, plus:

8. **`sorted_leq_nth` side conditions.** In recent MathComp, the
   `{in [pred n | n < size s] &, ...}` side conditions require explicit
   `rewrite inE` to unfold the `\in [pred ...]` wrapper before arithmetic
   rewrites like `Hsz_s` or `ltn_predL` can fire. The pattern is:
   ```
   have := @sorted_leq_nth _ leq leq_trans leqnn 0 (sort leq L) Hs.
   move=> /(_ i j); apply.
   + by rewrite inE ...   (* i < size (sort leq L) *)
   + by rewrite inE ...   (* j < size (sort leq L) *)
   + ...                   (* i <= j *)
   ```

9. **`nth_psi_left/right/inside` have explicit arguments.** Don't write
   `rewrite (nth_psi_left Hlt)` — that tries to supply the proof as
   the first (nat) argument. Use `rewrite !nth_psi_left //` or
   `rewrite [nth 0 (psi i w) k]nth_psi_left //`.

10. **`cmp_out_of_range` vs `cmp_out_of_range_left`.** The former compares
    `(elem > v)` (external value on the right); the latter compares
    `(v > elem)` (external value on the left). Choose based on which side
    of `<` the window element appears in the goal.

